---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getCopy, CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../lib/site";
const { lang = "en" } = Astro.props;
const c = getCopy(lang);
---
<Base lang={lang} title={c.privacy.title} description={c.privacy.description} path="/privacy/" ogImage="/og/page.jpg" ogAlt="Bad Leads">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="doc">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated 18 November 2026. Bad Leads is a detective game made by Murat Can Yüksel. This page explains what the game keeps, what the ads use, and how to reach us.</p>
      <h2>No account</h2>
      <p>You do not sign up or log in. We do not ask for your name, email address, phone number or precise location, and we do not keep a copy of your play on any system of ours.</p>
      <h2>Your progress stays on your device</h2>
      <p>The game saves your place, the clues you found and your settings on your own device only. We cannot see them. Choosing "Restart case" in the game's sound menu erases your saved progress, and deleting the app removes everything the game stored.</p>
      <h2>Ads</h2>
      <p>Bad Leads is free. It shows ads from Google AdMob when you choose to watch one for a hint. To show and measure these ads, Google may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your device's advertising ID</li>
        <li>your approximate location (a coarse location worked out from your IP address), which Google uses to choose and measure ads</li>
        <li>how you interact with an ad, such as whether it was shown, tapped or watched to the end</li>
        <li>diagnostic information, such as crash reports and performance data, meaning how well the game and the ads are working</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Google uses this information to show ads, measure them, prevent fraud, keep its ad service working and for analytics.</p>
      <p>We do not receive this information in a form that identifies you. Ads are personalised only if you agree. On iPhone and iPad, the game asks for your permission through Apple's App Tracking Transparency prompt before the advertising ID is used for personalised ads. You can change your answer at any time in Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Tracking. If you say no, you still see ads, but they are not tailored to you.</p>
      <h2>Who receives data</h2>
      <p>Google is the only company that receives data from the game. Google handles it under its own privacy policy and the data protection terms it applies to apps that use AdMob. We confirm that Google, as our only third party, provides the same or equal protection of your data as stated in this policy. We do not sell, share or send data to anyone else.</p>
      <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
      <p>We keep no personal data. Google keeps ad data for the periods set out in its retention policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/retention</a>.</p>
      <p>Google's own policy explains how it uses data from apps that use its services: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</p>
      <h2>Players where consent is required</h2>
      <p>If you play in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, Switzerland or another place where the law requires consent, the game shows Google's consent message before personalised ads, and it does not show Apple's tracking prompt, so your advertising ID is not used for tracking. You can accept or decline, and you can change your choice at any time under "Privacy choices" in the game's sound menu (the sliders button at the top right). Without your consent, only ads that are not personalised are shown.</p>
      <h2>Report an ad</h2>
      <p>If you see an ad that seems inappropriate or not suitable for teens, tap "Report an ad" in the game's sound menu, or write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the time you saw it and what the ad showed. We review every report and block the ad in AdMob where we can.</p>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Bad Leads is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child under 13 has given us personal information, write to us and we will help.</p>
      <h2>Asking us to delete data</h2>
      <p>We hold no personal data about you ourselves. Everything the game saves lives on your device, and "Restart case" or deleting the app removes it. For data that ad partners may hold about your advertising ID, you can reset or turn off the advertising ID in your device settings. If you would still like to ask us anything about your data, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we will reply.</p>
      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>If we change how the game handles data, we will update this page and its date.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Bad Leads, made by Murat Can Yüksel<br /><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
